There are n soldiers standing in a circle, numbered from 1 to n. Soldier 1 initially holds a sword. Starting from the soldier holding the sword:The soldier kills the next alive soldier in the clockwise direction.The sword is then passed to the next alive soldier after the killed soldier.The process continues until only one soldier remains alive.Initially, all the soldiers are alive. Determine the position (number) of the surviving soldier.Examples: Input: n = 5Output: 3Explanation: Initial circle: 1 2 3 4 51 kills 2: remaining: 1 3 4 53 kills 4: remaining: 1 3 55 kills 1: remaining: 3 53 kills 5: remaining: 3Input: n = 10Output: 5Explanation: After the first round, all even-numbered soldiers are eliminated.Remaining soldiers: 1 3 5 7 91 kills 3: remaining: 1 5 7 95 kills 7: remaining: 1 5 99 kills 1: remaining: 5 95 kills 9: remaining: 5 Try It YourselfTable of Content[Naive Approach] Using Circular Linked List - O(n) Time and O(n) Space[Better Approach] Using Josephus Recurrence - O(n) Time and O(1) Space[Expected Approach] Using Mathematical Observation - O(log n) Time and O(1) Space[Naive Approach] Using Circular Linked List - O(n) Time and O(n) SpaceThe ideas is to simulate the elimination process exactly as described. We first arrange all soldiers in a circular linked list so that the last soldier is connected back to the first. Starting from soldier 1, we repeatedly remove the next alive soldier and pass the sword to the following alive soldier. This process continues until only one soldier remains, whose position is the required answer.If there is only one soldier, return 1.Create a circular linked list containing soldiers numbered from 1 to n. Start the traversal from the first soldier. Repeatedly remove the next soldier from the circular list and pass the sword to the following alive soldier. Continue the elimination process until only one soldier remains in the circular list. Return the position of the remaining soldier.
            C++

    #include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

// Structure of a node in the circular linked list
class Node {
public:
    int data;
    Node *next;

    Node(int val)
    {
        data = val;
        next = nullptr;
    }
};

// Function to find the surviving soldier
int find(int n)
{
    // If there is only one soldier
    if (n == 1)
        return 1;

    // Create the first node
    Node *last = new Node(1);
    last->next = last;

    // Create the remaining nodes and form
    // a circular linked list
    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++)
    {
        Node *temp = new Node(i);
        temp->next = last->next;
        last->next = temp;
        last = temp;
    }

    // Start from the first soldier
    Node *curr = last->next;

    // Continue until only one soldier remains
    while (curr->next != curr)
    {
        // Soldier to be eliminated
        Node *victim = curr->next;

        // Remove the victim from the circle
        curr->next = victim->next;
        delete victim;

        // Pass the sword to the next alive soldier
        curr = curr->next;
    }

    // Store the surviving soldier
    int survivor = curr->data;
    delete curr;

    return survivor;
}

// Driver code
int main()
{
    int n = 5;
    cout << find(n) << endl;

    return 0;
}


